---
interface Props {
    avatarSrc?: string;
    avatarAlt?: string;
    ctaHref?: string;
    ctaLabel?: string;
}

const {
    avatarSrc = "/src/assets/developer.jpg",
    avatarAlt = "Charles, founder of post bridge",
    ctaHref  = "#",
    ctaLabel = "Try it for free",
} = Astro.props;
---

<section class="flex justify-center items-start px-4 sm:px-8 py-12 md:py-18 bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900" aria-label="Founder story">
    <div class="w-full max-w-2xl bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/50 border-3 border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-[20px] px-6 sm:px-12 py-10 sm:py-14 flex flex-col items-center gap-0">

        <div class="w-[90px] h-[90px] rounded-full overflow-hidden border-[3px] border-white dark:border-gray-800 shadow-[0_2px_12px_rgba(99,102,241,0.2)] dark:shadow-[0_2px_12px_rgba(99,102,241,0.3)] mb-2 flex-shrink-0 bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700" aria-hidden="true">
            <img
                    src={avatarSrc}
                    alt={avatarAlt}
                    class="w-full h-full object-cover block"
                    width="88"
                    height="88"
                    loading="lazy"
                    decoding="async"
            />
        </div>

        <div class="text-center mb-5">
            <h2 class="text-[1.35rem] font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 leading-tight mb-1">
                hey! it's <span class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400">Charles</span>
            </h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 font-normal">(the guy who made RareBooks)</p>
        </div>

        <div class="w-full flex flex-col gap-4 mb-9" role="article">
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                for <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">over half a decade</strong> i have worked closely with small and growing businesses helping them automate their business operations.
                i kept seeing the exact same problems everywhere.
            </p>
            <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 pl-0 list-none text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                <li>
                    business owners managing stock, sales and expenses with notebooks.
                </li>
                <li>
                    sales records written manually.
                </li>
                <li>
                    expenses tracked in spreadsheets.
                </li>
                <li>
                    employees <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">forgetting to record sales</strong> properly.
                </li>
                <li>
                    owners having <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">no clear visibility</strong> of what was happening in their own businesses <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">unless they were physically present.</strong>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                and when stock went missing, or profits didn't match expectations, they had to spend hours manually checking notebooks
                against shelves and warehouse stock just to figure out what happened.
                what surprised me most was this:
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                most existing softwares weren't actually built for these businesses.
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                the systems were too expensive, too complicated, and often required accounting or technical knowledge that many SMEs simply don't have.
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                many businesses employ hardworking people with <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">little or no technical background</strong> — not accountants, not analysts, not computer experts.
                they just needed something simple enough for anyone to use. something that helps the owner stay in control without needing to sit in the shop all day.
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                so <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">i built Rarebooks.</strong>
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                a simple business operating system designed specifically for SMEs.
                with Rarebooks, business owners can instantly know:
            </p>
            <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 pl-0 list-none text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                <li>
                    what stock was sold,
                </li>
                <li>
                    when stock is running low,
                </li>
                <li>
                    when new stock arrives,
                </li>
                <li>
                    daily revenues and expenses,
                </li>
                <li>
                    profit & loss,
                </li>
                <li>
                    and what's happening in the business even while they are away.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                employees don't need accounting degrees or advanced computer skills to use it.
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                the system is built to be simple, practical, and easy to operate from day one.
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                what started from observing the struggles of businesses during consulting has now become <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">a platform helping SMEs run with more clarity, accountability, and confidence.</strong>
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                because small businesses shouldn't need complicated enterprise software just to stay organized.
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                they deserve tools built for the reality of how they actually operate.
            </p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 m-0">
                and that's why Rarebooks exists.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex justify-center">
            <a href={ctaHref} class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-9 py-3.5 rounded-full bg-accent-600 hover:bg-accent-700 dark:bg-accent-600 dark:hover:bg-accent-500 text-white text-[0.925rem] font-semibold no-underline tracking-wide shadow-[0_2px_14px_rgba(99,102,241,0.32)] hover:shadow-[0_4px_20px_rgba(99,102,241,0.42)] transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 active:translate-y-0">
                {ctaLabel}
            </a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>